==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l Brave Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Li'l Dark Cat''' when obtained from [[Tiny Chopper (Deadly)|Li'l Axe Awakens!]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Due to being the Li'l version of a [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cat]], Li'l Axe Cat suffers from a severe lack of good basic stats, which makes him underperform greatly in his field. For this reason, usage of Li'l Axe Cat prior to unlocking his True Form is not recommended. However, including him in Row 1 with [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Cutter Cat]] will create one of the most efficient [[Cat Combo]]s in the game: [[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Brave Cutter]]. An Attack Up (Sm) for just two units is extremely helpful. Combined with [[Sister Act (Combo)|Sister Act]], you can achieve a greater bonus than [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]] while using the same number of slots!

==='''True Form'''===
Li'l Dark Cat greatly improves his stats and becomes anti-[[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]], but this doesn't help much due to his mediocre stats. His matchups against Angels are extremely poor, as he can only outrange [[Gabriel]], [[Divine Cyclone]] and [[St. Dober]]. Even as a meatshield he is outclassed by [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] (who is pretty much required to beat [[Tiny Chopper (Deadly)|Tiny Chopper]], the stage required for this True Form). Li'l Dark Cat is still stronger than his prior forms even against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies, so, if there is no other option but to use him due to circumstances (restrictions, somehow not owning anything better, etc.), there is never a reason to revert his form.

==='''Talents'''===
Li'l Dark Cat's '''Target [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]''' Talent combined with his '''Freeze''' Talent can make it a viable option in stages featuring Aku enemies that he can approach, as he can potentially paralyze them, and the chance isn't that low considering his disposability. However, the [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]] present in many such stages places a major handicap on Li'l Dark's stats, and his range continues to hinder his utility. '''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' can't do much to help with his low stats, and '''Resist Surge''' is equally pointless, as he doesn't have the health to tank any Surges.

==='''Orb'''===
Li'l Dark Cat has too low stats to make an effect orb do anything of note.
Death Mini-Surge or Single Surge Counter can give him a slight use to freeze crowds of Angels and Aku, but it's quite inconsistent, and you'd probably get better results from something else.

Resist Surge could see use when paired with the Target Aku and Resist Surge Talents, though that would be a large investment for a weaker Cactus.

